  "style": {
    "name": "Lapis Sun-Temple (Mesoamerican-Byzantine hybrid)",
    "rationale": "A warm orange terracotta wall skin framed by deep-blue lapis and glazed terracotta friezes, teal prismarine pilasters with gold capitals, a central pylon with a sun medallion, and a green oxidized-copper crown. Relief: wall skin at z=-1, core at z=-4..-2, projecting pilasters, cornices, and door frame at z=0. Openings are recessed by leaving the front layer unplaced, with glass or dark prismarine set behind. Bay rhythm is mirrored about x=15: pilasters at 2/6/9 and 21/24/28, windows at 3-5 and 7-8 and their mirrors, and a three-wide central portal with a stepped arch. Plinth at y0-1 in polished blackstone, cornice at y2 and y16, copper parapet at y17, crown at y23."
  },
